{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787876730498046001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"befuddled-gorilloid-mantisray","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f74ff8281587bc02630d1284d70f075f4278ee8ce761be8ea6a80732ec69d3c3","event_uuid":"c42ee8d1-4b87-483c-a07f-c0c1054063c3","position":{"commit_sha":"c694f48e6426bb8c79e56cea5bca3a892d1a2069","position":"1787866491109087731-c42ee8d1-4b87-483c-a07f-c0c1054063c3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"73aa27ed26bb71c7069db15c1a37e9ceb515fd40948782772ea1b0aaf0feea10","event_uuid":"180fa21a-d837-4bfc-a6ac-22cc55aa31a9","position":{"commit_sha":"34a679e1f29d478241a9c6ea54181778419763ad","position":"1787866757488045989-180fa21a-d837-4bfc-a6ac-22cc55aa31a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"74251ccb74c304f7c24c215b4221e143d95a6c79e23dcfd7ca8ce29eec04fac1","event_uuid":"9f7e4518-aeea-49af-b9a9-2dc9520247de","position":{"commit_sha":"b033e8fcc46647aa048850bf0d0161123ed7956c","position":"1787866916570859369-9f7e4518-aeea-49af-b9a9-2dc9520247de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787866491109087731,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"180fa21a-d837-4bfc-a6ac-22cc55aa31a9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAn MCP client cannot see CLI stderr, so the cross-session warning must ride in the\n**structured tool response** of single-ticket MCP tools. rebar already carries exactly this\nkind of advisory in structured responses: `WriteAckOut.description_warning`\n(`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:212`, populated via `_ack(..., description_warning=...)` at\n`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:60`). This story mirrors that pattern with a dedicated\ncross-session field on the single-ticket write and read responses, and leaves bulk-read\ntools untouched.\n\nDepends on the detector (`cross_session_warning_for`, sibling story) and the reducer\nclearing.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` field to the response models used by\nsingle-ticket MCP tools: `WriteAckOut` (`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:196`) for single-ticket\nwrites, and `TicketStateOut` (the model `show_ticket` returns, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:221`)\nfor the single-ticket read. Populate it from `cross_session_warning_for(ticket_id, ...)` in\nthe corresponding single-ticket handlers in `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` /\n`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` (extend the shared `_ack` helper to accept and thread the value,\nmatching how `description_warning` is threaded). Because the field defaults to `None`, the\n`outputSchema` gains an optional property and existing clients are unaffected (additive,\nback-compatible).\n\nThe single-ticket MCP tool set mirrors the CLI allowlist: `show_ticket`, `comment_ticket`,\n`edit_ticket`, `transition_ticket`, `reopen_ticket`, `tag_ticket`, `untag_ticket`,\n`set_file_impact`, `declare_no_file_impact`, `link_tickets` (primary `id1`),\n`unlink_tickets` (primary `id1`), `archive_ticket`, `check_ac`. The bulk read tools —\n`list_tickets`, `search`, `ready_tickets`, `next_batch` — do **not** populate the field.\n`claim_ticket` is excluded for the same reason as the CLI story (an already-`in_progress`\nticket fails the atomic claim before any warning). The warning reflects the ticket state\n**at operation time** (read before a mutation applies).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` — add `cross_session_warning: str | None = None` to\n  `WriteAckOut` and `TicketStateOut`.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` — thread the value through `_ack` and populate it in the\n  single-ticket write handlers.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` — populate it in the `show_ticket` handler.\n- `docs/mcp-reference.md` — document the new optional response field on the single-ticket\n  tools.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **contract test** — drive the real MCP handler functions in-process and assert on the\nvalidated response model (test-design §3 \"producer/consumer shape mismatch\": the real\nhandler produces the model through real `model_validate`). Use a real temporary tracker and\nset the acting session via `REBAR_SESSION_ID`.\n\n- With a ticket held by session A and acting session B, call the `show_ticket` handler and a\n  single-ticket write handler (e.g. `comment_ticket`); assert the returned model's\n  `cross_session_warning` is a non-empty string naming holder `A`.\n- Negative control (same session): acting as A, assert `cross_session_warning is None`.\n- Bulk exclusion: the `list_tickets` / `ready_tickets` responses have no populated\n  cross-session field for A's `in_progress` ticket.\n- Unset-id silence: with `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, the single-ticket handlers return\n  `cross_session_warning is None`.\n- Schema check: the tool's advertised `outputSchema` includes the optional\n  `cross_session_warning` property (asserted against the generated schema), and a default\n  response (no mismatch) still validates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `show_ticket` and a single-ticket write handler (`comment_ticket`) return a model\n  whose `cross_session_warning` names holder `A` when acting as session B against an\n  A-held ticket (checked by an in-process MCP contract test under `make test`).\n- [ ] Negative control: acting as session A, `cross_session_warning is None` on the same\n  handlers (checked by the same test).\n- [ ] `list_tickets` / `ready_tickets` responses do not populate a cross-session warning for\n  A's `in_progress` ticket (checked by a bulk-exclusion assertion).\n- [ ] With `REBAR_SESSION_ID` unset, single-ticket handlers return `cross_session_warning is\n  None` (checked by an unset-id assertion).\n- [ ] `WriteAckOut` and `TicketStateOut` `outputSchema` expose the optional\n  `cross_session_warning` property and existing (unset) responses still validate (checked by\n  a schema/model-validation assertion).\n- [ ] `docs/mcp-reference.md` documents the field (checked: `grep -n \"cross_session_warning\"\n  docs/mcp-reference.md` matches).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"add cross_session_warning field to WriteAckOut and TicketStateOut"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"thread the warning through _ack and populate it in single-ticket write handlers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"populate cross_session_warning in the show_ticket handler"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"document the new optional response field"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","0804-9a6b-9182-42c9"],["parent","1aca-695f-a0a4-4236"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"734d-0998-c47c-48d9","ticket_type":"story","title":"MCP: carry cross_session_warning in single-ticket tool responses","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c42ee8d1-4b87-483c-a07f-c0c1054063c3","180fa21a-d837-4bfc-a6ac-22cc55aa31a9","9f7e4518-aeea-49af-b9a9-2dc9520247de"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787876730498046001,"uuid":"77110b55-9049-4ce7-ab16-07cb43ac3214"}